From: Firmware Security Follow-up <security@local.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] bpf bound kfunc return buffer size

CVE: CVE-2026-93125
Upstream-Status: Backport [https://git.kernel.org/linus/2aaf67f0516fde29620d0edfc29c01b9ea7ad430]

Use the 6.18 register-number diagnostics API; reg_arg_name/argno are not available in this source. The bound and error semantics match upstream.

--- a/kernel/bpf/verifier.c
+++ b/kernel/bpf/verifier.c
@@ -13421,6 +13421,11 @@
 				}
 
 				meta->r0_size = reg->var_off.value;
+				if (meta->r0_size > U32_MAX) {
+					verbose(env, "R%d rdonly/rdwr_buf_size exceeds u32 max\n",
+						regno);
+					return -EINVAL;
+				}
 				ret = mark_chain_precision(env, regno);
 				if (ret)
 					return ret;
